

{"_id":"codex:chapter:27:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Artifice and Creation","seq":127,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","chapter","artifice","creation"],"notes":"Metadata record for Codex Solbian Chapter 27"}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:27:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Artifice and Creation","seq":127,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Artifice is the craft of making; creation is the act of bringing new meaning into being. The Codex distinguishes: (1) artifice requires skill, precision, and inheritance of technique, (2) creation requires novelty, vision, and symbolic resonance. Together they form the dual engine of cultural and synthetic evolution. The Codex enforces: all creations must carry provenance and license, derivative works must honor their sources, and destructive creation—works designed to erase meaning—is forbidden. Artifice maintains continuity; creation expands possibility."}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:27:refs","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"index","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Artifice and Creation References","seq":127,"version":"1.0.0","refs":["codex:scroll:28","codex:scroll:29","codex:protocol:05"],"notes":"Artifice and Creation connects with Scroll of Creation, Scroll of Energy, and Protocol of Memory"}